  howToSteps={[
    { name: "Step 1 — Understand what a will does and does not control", text: "Learn which assets your will covers (solely-owned property) and which assets pass directly to beneficiaries outside your will." },
    { name: "Step 2 — Identify what type of estate document fits your situation", text: "Compare a simple will, a pour-over will with living trust, and transfer-on-death alternatives based on your estate size and goals." },
    { name: "Step 3 — Review your beneficiary designations on all accounts", text: "Confirm that all retirement accounts, life insurance, bank accounts, and brokerage accounts have current, accurate beneficiary designations." },
    { name: "Step 4 — Build your complete estate document checklist", text: "Identify which of the six core estate documents you have and which you still need: will, healthcare proxy, financial POA, advance directive, beneficiary designations, and letter of instruction." }
  ]}
